Inventory graph|ansible-inventory -i inventory.yml --graph|Resolves inventory and displays group membership.|Review the exact fleet before running a play.|Group branches show membership; unexpected hosts indicate inventory or filter problems.|@web: ... host1 ... host2|Read-only discovery may call external inventory APIs; inspect a trusted inventory source.
Host variables|ansible-inventory -i inventory.yml --host HOST|Prints resolved inventory variables for one host.|Find connection settings or unexpected variable values.|JSON keys show inventory-derived values, not every later play-level override.|{"ansible_host":"192.0.2.10"}|Can reveal secrets; replace HOST and protect output.
List play targets|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --list-hosts|Lists hosts matched by each play without executing its tasks.|Verify host patterns and limits before changes.|Read the play name, pattern and host count for every play.|hosts (2): host1 host2|Inventory plugins may execute discovery; use trusted project files.
List tasks|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --list-tasks|Shows statically discoverable tasks selected by a playbook.|Review order and scope before execution.|Dynamic includes may not expose every eventual task in this view.|tasks: Install package ... Configure service ...|Does not execute normal tasks; not a complete prediction of dynamic behavior.
Syntax validation|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --syntax-check|Parses and checks playbook syntax.|Catch malformed YAML and structural issues early.|Success normally prints the playbook name; failures identify parsing context.|playbook: site.yml|Does not validate every runtime variable, remote command or application configuration.
Check mode|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --check --limit CANARY|Requests predicted changes on a limited target set.|Preview supported operations before a real rollout.|changed means a predicted change for supporting modules; skipped tasks may reduce coverage.|PLAY RECAP ... changed=1 failed=0|Not a universal dry run; modules and tasks can have exceptions, so review trusted content and use a safe canary.
Check with diff|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --check --diff --limit CANARY|Adds supported before/after diffs to check-mode output.|Review rendered configuration changes.|Lines prefixed - are removed and + are added; inspect paths and values.|--- before ... +++ after|Diffs can expose secrets; disable diff on sensitive tasks.
Module documentation|ansible-doc ansible.builtin.template|Displays the installed module's options, behavior and examples.|Confirm parameters and check-mode support for the actual installed version.|Read required fields, attributes and return values before using conditions.|OPTIONS ... ATTRIBUTES ... RETURN VALUES|Local read-only documentation lookup.
Collection versions|ansible-galaxy collection list|Lists installed collections and versions.|Reproduce a controller environment and diagnose version differences.|Multiple installation paths may contain different versions; note the path headings.|Collection Version ... ansible.posix ...|Read-only; compare with project requirements.
Connectivity test|ansible -i inventory.yml CANARY -m ansible.builtin.ping|Tests Ansible connection and Python execution on selected hosts.|Distinguish transport or interpreter problems from playbook logic.|pong means module execution succeeded; unreachable indicates connection-level failure.|HOST SUCCESS => {"ping":"pong"}|Not ICMP ping; runs a module on the authorized target.
Gather selected facts|ansible -i inventory.yml CANARY -m ansible.builtin.setup -a 'filter=ansible_distribution*'|Collects filtered operating-system facts.|Check platform assumptions used by roles.|Returned ansible_facts show distribution and version fields available on the host.|"ansible_distribution": "Debian"|Runs read-oriented fact gathering remotely; scope targets and protect inventory details.
List tags|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --list-tags|Shows tags available for task selection.|Understand supported partial-run entry points.|TASK TAGS identifies selectable labels; dependencies may still be omitted by selective execution.|TASK TAGS: [config, packages]|Read-only task discovery; test tag combinations before production use.
Ansible version and paths|ansible --version|Reports ansible-core version and active configuration paths.|Reproduce differences between a developer workstation and CI.|config file, module paths and Python version explain the controller environment.|ansible [core VERSION] config file = /project/ansible.cfg|Read-only; does not contact inventory hosts.
Changed configuration settings|ansible-config dump --only-changed|Displays non-default effective Ansible configuration.|Find an unexpected inventory, connection or privilege setting.|Entries show setting names and origins where supported; environment variables can override file values.|DEFAULT_HOST_LIST(/project/ansible.cfg) = ...|Read-only controller inspection; output can expose internal paths or configuration values.
Configuration source file|ansible-config view|Prints the active Ansible configuration file.|Inspect project configuration without guessing which file is in use.|This is file content, not every resolved environment override; compare with dump for effective values.|[defaults] ...|Read-only; configuration may include sensitive paths or plugin settings.
Full resolved inventory|ansible-inventory -i inventory.yml --list|Outputs resolved inventory as structured JSON.|Inspect groups and host variables before applying a play.|_meta.hostvars contains host variables; groups contain hosts and children. Dynamically supplied variables may include secrets.|{"_meta":{"hostvars":{...}},"web":{"hosts":[...]}}|Read-only host inspection, but inventory plugins can call external APIs; protect exported variables.
Host pattern preview|ansible -i inventory.yml 'web:&staging' --list-hosts|Shows hosts matching the intersection of two groups.|Validate a narrowed target pattern before remote execution.|The count and names are the resolved target set; group names alone are not an access control.|hosts (2): web-staging-1 web-staging-2|Read-only inventory resolution; keep the shell quotes around the pattern.
Module inventory|ansible-doc --list|Lists modules discoverable by the controller.|Find available modules and identify missing collections.|Each line names a module and brief description; presence does not guarantee remote requirements are installed.|ansible.builtin.copy Copy files to remote locations|Read-only; collection paths and versions affect results.
Module task examples|ansible-doc --snippet ansible.builtin.service|Prints a task-oriented parameter skeleton for a module.|Start from documented parameter names rather than guessing syntax.|Commented fields describe options; required fields must still be supplied and examples reviewed.|- name: ... ansible.builtin.service: ...|Read-only; a generated snippet is not a tested production task.
Collection installation|ansible-galaxy collection install -r requirements.yml|Installs collections declared in a requirements file.|Reproduce reviewed automation dependencies on a clean controller.|Installation messages name collection versions and destination paths; inspect the requirements file for intended pins.|Installing 'namespace.collection:VERSION'|Downloads executable automation content; use reviewed trusted collections and version constraints.
Collection metadata|ansible-galaxy collection list --format json|Emits installed collection versions as JSON.|Record the automation toolchain in a CI diagnostic artifact.|Paths group installed collections and their versions; multiple paths may contain different versions.|{"/path/collections":{"namespace.collection":{"version":"..."}}}|Read-only; inspect actual search order if duplicate versions exist.
Role installation|ansible-galaxy role install -r roles/requirements.yml|Installs role dependencies from a declared requirements file.|Set up a reproducible role-based project.|Messages identify installed role versions or revisions; an unpinned source can change later.|- extracting role_name to roles/role_name|Downloads executable task content; use reviewed sources and pins.
Encrypt a variable file|ansible-vault encrypt group_vars/all/secrets.yml|Encrypts a plaintext variable file with Vault.|Protect stored secret content before committing it.|The encrypted file begins with a Vault header; successful encryption does not remove prior plaintext history or logs.|Encryption successful|Mutates the file and prompts for a Vault secret. Keep secure recovery access and rotate already-exposed credentials.
View encrypted content|ansible-vault view group_vars/all/secrets.yml|Decrypts a Vault file for display without rewriting it.|Inspect authorized secret content when necessary.|Output is plaintext, not masked values; the command's success only confirms decryption.|Decrypted YAML displayed on the terminal|Sensitive read; use a private terminal and never redirect the output into shared CI logs.
Edit encrypted content|ansible-vault edit group_vars/all/secrets.yml|Opens decrypted content in an editor and re-encrypts on save.|Maintain an authorized Vault-protected variable file.|The editor shows plaintext during editing; inspect the final file header after saving.|Vault file saved after editor exit|Mutates secrets; secure editor swap/backup handling and use the intended Vault identity.
Change Vault encryption key|ansible-vault rekey group_vars/all/secrets.yml|Re-encrypts a Vault file using a new Vault secret.|Rotate access to stored encrypted content.|Rekey successful refers to the file encryption key, not the application credentials stored inside.|Rekey successful|Mutates encryption; update authorized consumers securely and preserve a recovery path.
Canary execution|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --limit CANARY|Runs the playbook on the explicitly limited host pattern.|Apply a reviewed change to a small representative target set.|PLAY RECAP shows ok, changed, unreachable and failed; zero failed is not a substitute for service postconditions.|CANARY : ok=12 changed=2 unreachable=0 failed=0|Mutates remote hosts according to all selected tasks. Preview hosts and check availability before execution.
Privilege-scoped execution|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml maintenance.yml --limit CANARY --ask-become-pass|Runs a reviewed maintenance play and prompts for an escalation password where become is configured.|Use an interactive authorized privilege path without putting passwords in shell arguments.|Escalation applies according to the play/task settings; a prompt does not mean every task should run as root.|BECOME password: then task results|May change privileged host state. Use task-scoped become and protect the interactive session.
Validate tagged path|ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml site.yml --tags deploy --list-tasks|Lists tasks selected for a tagged execution path.|Check whether prerequisites are omitted before a partial rollout.|The task list reflects tag selection; dynamic includes may not reveal every runtime task in this preview.|tasks: ... TAGS: [deploy]|Read-only planning aid; test the selected path in a representative environment.
Read-only remote command|ansible -i inventory.yml CANARY -m ansible.builtin.command -a 'uptime'|Runs uptime on a deliberately scoped remote target.|Verify connection context and inspect current load without a shell pipeline.|stdout contains remote uptime/load; Ansible command may report CHANGED despite this command being observational.|CANARY CHANGED rc=0 ... load average ...|Connects to hosts; the example is read-only, but command can execute arbitrary actions. Use a verified host pattern.
